1
00:00:02,380 --> 00:00:10,230
Lesson 23. Bob has a surprise visitor. Bob's former boss Peter from the furniture store

2
00:00:10,080 --> 00:00:15,970
comes to visit. He offers Bob his old job back, but Bob's not interested.

3
00:00:17,140 --> 00:00:20,229
Hi Bob, I was just in the neighborhood so I thought I'd stop by.

4
00:00:20,800 --> 00:00:25,279
Come on in. Take a cookie. Thanks. I'm glad to see you're not holding a

5
00:00:25,129 --> 00:00:30,339
wedge against me for firing you. Not at all. At first it burned me up, but I feel

6
00:00:30,190 --> 00:00:34,820
better. Good. I'm glad you have no hard feelings. How would you like your old

7
00:00:34,670 --> 00:00:40,079
job back? What happened to your wonderful new manager? She drank the twerk. By

8
00:00:39,929 --> 00:00:43,719
five o'clock she'd be lying under a dining room table. Three seats to the wind.

9
00:00:44,189 --> 00:00:49,359
Yesterday I finally got rid of her. Let me get this straight. You replaced me with

10
00:00:49,210 --> 00:00:55,100
some crazy woman who got plastered every day on the job. Yes, I lost my head.

11
00:00:55,469 --> 00:00:59,539
I don't think you lost your head. I just think you've got rocks in your head.

12
00:01:00,030 --> 00:01:05,260
Bob, I'm trying to level with you. I never should have let you go. No use crying

13
00:01:05,109 --> 00:01:10,980
over spilt milk. So you'll come back and work for me? Not in your life. Susan and I

14
00:01:10,829 --> 00:01:14,820
are very well off now. We just sold our new company for a small fortune.

